# Typed param guard failure: fn [let x@Integer] called with String.
# The clause has a type guard on x: the clause only fires if arg.type_id() == TYPE_ID_INT.
# Passing a String fails the guard. With a single-clause fn, no clause matches →
# the evaluator raises a no-match error that includes the actual argument type.
[f: [fn [let x@Integer] [+ x 1]]]
[f "hello"]
=== error
no matching clause for the given arguments
